  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"A booking sheet lists bench sessions, and all unclaimed sessions remain available to arriving members.\", \"decision\": \"How should members obtain bench time?\", \"goal\": \"Help members make steady progress while sharing tools, work surfaces, materials, and responsibility for the studio.\", \"problem\": \"A neighborhood craft studio serves members working on small personal projects. It has bookable benches, ordinary hand tools, shared consumables, a drying rack, labeled storage, a message board, and a steward during opening hours. Members follow the same basic safety rules. Helpers can support brief activities without taking over the whole room, and each decision concerns a separate routine.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nThe steward publishes a rotating order for members to claim bench sessions on the booking sheet. Earlier access changes between booking rounds while members still choose among the sessions available to them.\nMembers enter preferred bench sessions on the booking sheet, and the steward assigns available sessions each morning. The steward can spread competing requests before members commit to their working times.\nMembers claim available bench sessions directly on the booking sheet before beginning their work. The sheet gives members immediate control of their schedules while showing everyone which sessions are already taken."
    }
  ],
